soba noodle is our tradition to eat  during new year's eve  toshikoshi soba means ear crossing  noodles  some people say one of the reason is  this buddhist temples  used to give sober to poor people on new  year's  and it's become a tradition to eat on  new year's eve  so what i know about this tradition i  saw soba noodle is very easy to prepare  and end of the year it's very busy  so they want to make a meal something  very quickly and easy  i'm not hundred percent sure what is the  origin story  if somebody knows please let me know so  one of our superstitions  is so far it's long so it's like  longevity of life  to eat soba noodle it's kind of good  luck thing  if you eat long soba noodles you will  have a longer life there's a bunch of  different superstitions about it too  sugar noodles are made with buckwheat so  it's gluten free  it has no gluten in it so it's very  difficult to make a home you need a  skill to make soba  if you want to know more about making  soba noodles  watch alvin's video the art of making  soba noodles  it's very beautiful video you can also  purchase the dried soba noodle  in the asian market or some grocery  stores  so one of the topping in the video is  called kaki again  it's type of tempura it's like veggie  medley bunch of different vegetables  coated with tempura butter and fried  usually you also include onion and  carrots  soda is usually either soft hot or cold  depending on the weather or your mood  cold soba come with dipping sauce  sort of like tsukemen noodle and warm  soba  come submerged in soup more like a ramen  or udon  yaksoda also has soda in their name  but it's completely different  ingredients  so yaki means punk fried for yakisoba  soba  is baku noodle last time i had a soba  noodle  i went with water team in tokyo someone  requested  soba and it turns out they're a famous  sofa shop nearby  and we went but we waited for 30 minutes  but it was really good  totally worth it i also ate soba noodles  when we shop in new york  i like eating soba noodles in the summer  time usually cold  because it's refreshing and light for  the winter time i like  warm soba noodles i usually will eat  soba noodles for new year's eve  it's a great way of connecting my  culture and my tradition  in my current life in l.a  [Music]  you
 

